window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>When the world unraveled, Kade found purpose in the pieces.</b></p> <p>When the System rewrites reality, nineteen-year-old Kade is left with no home, no allies, and a power he doesn’t understand—an ability to forge living demons from ether, shaped by will and resolve. In a land ruled by death and dominance, strength is survival, and weakness is a death sentence.</p> <p>But power isn’t enough.</p> <p>As Kade builds his army, he draws the attention of a ruthless warlord who sees him not as an enemy, but as a threat to the natural order. Every demon costs him something. Every victory comes with blood. And every step forward blurs the line between the man he believes himself to be—and the monster the world already sees.</p> <p><i>Forged in Flesh</i> is a dark LitRPG fantasy about what remains when the world burns—and what you’re willing to become to survive it.</p> <p>Perfect for fans of grimdark fantasy, LitRPG progression, and post-apocalyptic worlds where survival demands sacrifice, <i>Forged in Flesh</i> delivers a tale that fuses the tension of an apocalypse with the brutal psychology of an antihero’s rise. The System has rewritten reality, scattering monsters across a broken Earth and leaving shattered towns to fend for themselves. In this new order, power isn’t a gift—it’s a cost, and every choice leaves scars. Kade’s path is one of blood, demons, and impossible decisions, where the line between man and monster erodes with every step.</p> <p>Listeners who crave morally gray characters, relentless world-building, and progression that feels earned will find themselves drawn into a story where connection is as perilous as combat and trust deadlier than steel. <i>Forged in Flesh</i> is more than survival—it is fire carried through the ashes, no matter how much of your soul it consumes.</p>"; 
